  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Walsh Federal obligated $357M in FY2026 to date across 20 awards, with an average award size of $17.8M and year-over-year obligations up 10.0%. Walsh Federal's FY2026 obligations are concentrated in building construction work, and current-year totals are partial because the figures reflect fiscal year to date activity. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer this fiscal year, having obligated $277M, followed by the Department of Transportation, which obligated $79.4M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction dominates Walsh Federal's market presence at $356M in FY2026 to date, while Industrial Building Construction accounts for $325K. Walsh Federal's obligations have varied by fiscal year, with $120M in FY21, $265M in FY22, $699M in FY23, $251M in FY24, $324M in FY25, and $357M in FY26. These facts show a firm whose federal portfolio is concentrated in a narrow set of large construction awards and heavily weighted to specific agencies in the current fiscal year.",
